nd Classical periods and he is recognised for many innovations.", "extract_html": "<p><b>Johann Wenzel Anton Stamitz</b> was a Czech composer and violinist. Stamitz is considered the founding father of the Mannheim school, a composition style that his two surviving sons, Carl and Anton Stamitz, continued. His music is stylistically transitional between the Baroque and Classical periods and he is recognised for many innovations.</p>"}